    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d518">

                <pb facs="0639" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg571"/>

                <head>Count Wydenbruck to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 11, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: I thank you for your
                    obliging communication of the 9th instant, (8th.) As soon as the answer to
                    Captain Roe’s application shall be known to you, may I hope that you may have
                    the goodness to have it telegraphed to me, in order that my court may be
                    informed of its tenor without loss of time ?</p>
                <p>I have the honor to remain, Mr. Secretary of State, with the highest
                    consideration, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WYDENBRUCK.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
